(
Morse trainer
-------------

In order to train my ears for Morse characters and words, I want to build
a "bug" type of Morse key, with a single blade in the center and two contact
points, one on each side, one for dits and one for dahs. 

The key then handles timing, in that as long as a contact is closed, it
repeats dits or dahs at correct length and inbetween space, as well as 
inbetween symbol time (one dit long).

This eliminates the issue of "button bounce", both because I will not use
buttons, but just contact points, so no springs involved, but also because
once detecting a contact on one of the points, it will generate the symbol,
and space following it, before checking the points again.

I also want to display the characters on an LCD display (I2C), and implement
a simple menu system for setting the speed. 


)

: Chars
	s" __ETIANMSURWDKGOHVF_L_PJBXCYZQ__54_3___2__+____16=/___(_7___8_90____________?________.____@______-___________)_____,"
;

63 constant UNKNOWN ( ? )

5 constant PinDit
6 constant PinDah
7 constant PinBeep
13 constant PinLed

variable msTick

: Init
	PinDit IN Pin .setIn
	PinDah IN Pin .setIn
	PinBeep IN Pin .setOut
	PinLed IN Pin .setOut
	
	60 msTick !   (length of dit in millis at 20 wpm)
	
	(-- using timer 0 --)
	0 IN Timers .set
;

: ShowChar (value --)
	dup Chars c@ >= &1 jmp?          (-- is value out of bounds? --)
	Chars + 1+ c@ emit
	ret
	/1 (-- out of bounds --)
		drop
		UNKNOWN emit
;

(-- test --)
: ShowR b1010 ShowChar ;


(-- wait for ticks to pass, timer #0 --)
: Wait (ticks --)
	msTick @ * delay
;

: SoundOn
	500 PinBeep IN Pin .writeAnalog
	1 PinLed IN Pin .writeDigital
;

: SoundOff
	0 PinBeep IN Pin .writeDigital
	0 PinLed IN Pin .writeDigital
;

: Play (ticks --)
	(ticks)
	SoundOn
	Wait
	SoundOff
	(-- pause after symbol --)
	1 Wait
;

(-- test --)
: test
	Init
	/1
		key? ret?
		1 Play
		3 Play
		1 Play
		3 Wait
		&1 jmp
;


